## Code Example
```javascript
function redact(customer, level) {
  if (level === 'full') return { name: null, email: null, card: null };
  if (level === 'partial') {
    const maskedCard = customer.card.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
    const maskedEmail = customer.email.replace(/([^@]{1,2})[^@]*(@.*)/, (m, p1, p2) => p1[0] + '**' + p2);
    return { ...customer, card: maskedCard, email: maskedEmail };
  }
  return customer;
}
```

Why This Is Asked

Tests practical multi-tenant isolation, per-tenant offset management, and resilience in KCNA with simple backpressure and testing.

Key Concepts

- Per-tenant isolation and routing
- Token-bucket rate limiting per tenant
- Durable per-tenant offsets and recovery
- Idempotent processing with robust retries
- Lightweight test harness simulating downstream lag

Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: per-tenant rate limiter and offset store
class TenantState {
  constructor(tenant, rate) {
    this.tenant = tenant;
    this.offsets = new Map(); // topic -> offset
    this.limiter = new TokenBucket(rate); // per-tenant rate
  }
  canConsume() { return this.limiter.tryConsume(this.tenant); }
  commitOffset(topic, offset) { this.offsets.set(topic, offset); }
}
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate) {
    this.rate = rate; this.tokens = rate; this.last = Date.now();
  }
  tryConsume() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.rate, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= 1) { this.tokens -= 1; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you persist offsets across restarts and recover after crash?
- How would you scale the rate limiter across many tenants?
- What metrics would you collect to detect backlog per tenant?

## Why This Question Matters
This question tests your ability to handle late data gracefully without breaking at-least-once delivery guarantees. It probes your understanding of per-topic state management, routing decisions under delayed data conditions, and offset tracking.

## Key Concepts
- Per-topic watermarks for independent time-window tracking
- Late data routing based on watermark thresholds
- Offset tracking and message deduplication for at-least-once semantics
- Canary testing to validate both in-order and late-data paths

## Code Example
```javascript
class WatermarkManager {
  constructor(maxLagMs = 60000) {
    this.maxLagMs = maxLagMs;
    this.topicWatermarks = new Map();
    this.offsetStore = new Map();
  }

  processMessage(topic, partition, offset, timestamp) {
    const key = `${topic}-${partition}`;
    const currentWatermark = this.topicWatermarks.get(key) || 0;

    if (timestamp > currentWatermark) {
      this.topicWatermarks.set(key, timestamp);
    }

    const watermark = this.topicWatermarks.get(key);
    const lag = watermark - timestamp;

    this.offsetStore.set(key, offset);

    if (lag > this.maxLagMs) {
      return { route: 'late_events', topic, partition, offset };
    }

    return { route: 'main', topic, partition, offset };
  }
}
```

This implementation maintains per-topic watermarks, routes late messages appropriately, tracks offsets, and supports at-least-once delivery through committed offset storage.

